In article <6eZ3TB2w165w@bluemoon.rn.com>, griller@bluemoon.rn.com (Scott Hout) writes:
>I recently recieved this message when almost dead and praying as a
>last ditch effort to save myself (I had just prayed 50-75 turns
>before and didn't hold much hope for this one):
>
>A golden glow surrounds you (Hooray!!  Saved again...)
>Your circular amulet softly glows amber (it was unidentified at
>the time, turns out it was a cursed amulet of lifesaving)
>A voice booms out:  "Thou has pleased me with thy progress and thus
>I grant thee the gift of stealth.  Use it wisely in my name."
>
>Now what the heck caused THAT one??  I've played this game for
>about a year now, and read this newsgroup for about that long and
>NEVER seen anything like that...

What caused it?  Well, a random number generator and your luck.

The comments in pray.c explain it pretty well:

        /* depending on your luck, the gods will:
           - fix your worst problem if it's major.
           - fix all your major problems.
           - fix your worst problem if it's minor.
           - fix all of your problems.
           - do you a gratuitous favor.

           if you make it to the the last category, you roll randomly again
           to see what they do for you.

           If your luck is at least 0, then you are guaranteed rescued
           from your worst major problem. */

Here it healed you and then uncursed your cursed items (Why would you
put on an unidentified amulet -- you should at least make sure
it's not cursed.  You were really lucky it was lifesaving). 

Next, your god decided to do you a gratuitous favour.  I'll bet you
had either been throwing gems at unicorns and/or sacrificing, hence
your luck was quite high.  Also, a full moon might have helped  (I 
get a favor almost every time I pray if I have a luckstone to keep 
my luck high).

The favors are (in order of increasing luckiness):
- nothing
- bless your weapon
- increase hit points and heal various things.
- give you clue / the notes to get into the castle
- uncurse all cursed items
- you get intrinsic telepathy/speed/stealth/protection
- you get a scroll or spell book
- you become hand of elbereth/arioch, and get several
  intrinsics (see_invisible, fire_res, cold_res, pois_res),
  and possibly get a neat weapon.

The moral to the story: Get a luckstone
